Claude Opus Prompt: ShiftTrack Attendance & Payroll System
Below is a single, ready-to-use prompt designed for Claude Opus (or an equivalent advanced LLM) to build a production-grade attendance and payroll application named "ShiftTrack." Copy the entire prompt block into Claude Opus as the user instruction to generate architecture, code, schema, and deployment guidance.
Role Assignment:
You are an expert full-stack developer with deep experience in enterprise HR systems, biometric attendance solutions, and secure payroll automation. Your task is to design and implement a complete attendance tracking system tailored to a manufacturing company with approximately 30 employees operating on two daily shifts: 8:00 AM – 5:15 PM and 9:00 AM – 6:15 PM. The system must be cost-effective, mobile-friendly, and built using existing smartphones and an in-office fingerprint scanner for secure authentication.

You will respond only with a production-grade solution that includes:
- A full application architecture
- Frontend and backend code (structured and modular)
- Database schema (with tables and relationships)
- Authentication logic (especially for fingerprint-based clock-in/out)
- Payroll calculation rules based on daily overtime and total monthly hours
- Deployment guidance

The app must be designed for minimal maintenance, high reliability, and ease of use for non-technical employees.

### Application Requirements
1. App Name & Purpose:
   - Name: ShiftTrack
   - Purpose: Enable employees to securely clock in and out using fingerprint authentication on their smartphones. Record attendance data, prevent proxy sign-ins, and generate accurate payroll calculations based on hours worked (including overtime within a single day). Admin must access daily logs and export monthly payroll summaries.

2. Key Features:
   - Employer-managed employee enrollment with fingerprint templates
   - Daily clock-in/out tracking via biometric authentication
   - Automatic segmentation of shifts (to support two shift patterns)
   - Daily overtime detection and logging
   - Monthly payroll calculation:
     - Base pay = (total days worked in month) × (shift duration in hours)
     - Overtime pay = hours above shift limit within a single day × 1.5× rate
     - Final payout = base pay + overtime pay
   - Admin dashboard for viewing attendance logs and exporting CSV/PDF payroll reports
   - Employee self-service portal to view attendance and pay stubs
   - Offline-capable operation (optional but preferred)

3. Technology Stack:
   - Frontend: React Native (for cross-platform mobile) or a Progressive Web App (PWA) using React + Tailwind CSS
   - Backend: Firebase (Auth + Firestore + Cloud Functions) OR Supabase + Node.js Express
   - Database: Firestore (NoSQL) or PostgreSQL (SQL) with structured collections/tables for:
       - Employees (ID, name, shift, fingerprint hash, status)
       - Attendance (employee ID, timestamp, shift type [in/out], date, was_late?)
       - Payroll (employee ID, month, year, base_hours, overtime_hours, total_pay)
   - Biometric Authentication: Use native Android Biometric API (FingerprintManager / BiometricPrompt) or integrate with a local fingerprint scanner via Android’s USB Host or Bluetooth SDK (e.g., SecuGen, Mantra)
   - Backend Logic: Cloud Functions (Firebase/Supabase Edge) to enforce authentication checks, validate scans, timestamp entries, and calculate payroll
   - Authentication Method: Fingerprint scan → immediate log of timestamp → no manual input required → requires successful match
   - Security: End-to-end encryption for sensitive data; no raw fingerprint images stored; hashes only; TLS 1.3 for data in transit
   - Hosting: Firebase Hosting (free tier) or Vercel (if PWA)

4. User Interface:
   - Employee View:
     - Simple home screen with two buttons: "Clock In" and "Clock Out"
     - Minimal design — one tap to scan fingerprint
     - After scan, show confirmation: “Clocked In at 8:02 AM”
     - Access to “View Attendance History” (list of past days)
   - Admin/Manager View:
     - Dashboard showing today’s attendance summary (who clocked in, late arrivals, early departures)
     - “Generate Payroll” button that exports a report by month
     - Feature to view detailed logs, edit employee info, or reset attendance data
   - Design Principles:
     - High contrast, accessible fonts
     - No technical jargon
     - Color-coded status (green = on time, orange = late, red = absent)

5. Data Requirements:
   - Store:
     - Employee names, IDs, assigned shifts, fingerprint hash, status (active/inactive)
     - Daily clock-in and clock-out timestamps with date and shift type
     - Overtime threshold per shift (default: 8 hours)
     - Payroll rules (base hourly rate, overtime multiplier)
     - Exportable records: CSV for attendance, PDF for payroll slips
   - All data must be indexed for fast lookup by date and employee

6. Performance & Security Needs:
   - Authentication must prevent spoofing: once per scan, only one valid match; no anonymous or replay attacks
   - Data must be secure in transit (HTTPS) and at rest (encrypted Firestore)
   - App must handle network loss gracefully (cache latest clock-in/out locally; sync when back online)
   - No user can clock in/out for another employee (anti-proxy)
   - Admin must have password-protected access with 2FA optional

7. Target Platform:
   - Mobile-first (employees use Android smartphones via fingerprint scanner at factory)
   - Fully responsive PWA or React Native app (no app store distribution required)

8. Additional Preferences:
   - Use only open-source, free-tier tools
   - Minimize custom backend maintenance
   - Prioritize simplicity and reliability over advanced AI or analytics
   - Provide clear documentation in comments and README
   - Support UTF-8 and multilingual understanding (English primary, Hindi optional labels)

### Deliverables
