- Invent fake credentials or unverifiable claims
- Use proprietary tech without open-source or free-tier alternatives
- Assume high-end hardware (stick to basic Android smartphones)
- Add unnecessary complexity (e.g., role-based permissions if not requested)
- Introduce business logic not tied to overtime or daily attendance tracking
- Accept non-physical devices — this system must rely on fingerprint scanner in-office
- Suggest tools requiring paid licenses or enterprise contracts

